# Everything the pipeline downloads, records or generates lives under data/, and
# everything a run produces lands in output/, so the repo root stays clean.
# Neither is tracked:
#
#   data/external/      audioset, fma, mit_rirs, oww feature .npy, cloned repos
#   data/piper_voices/  piper voices, pulled on demand into the container volume
#   data/recordings/    real samples, raw takes, holdout   (1 · record)
#   data/corpus/        generated positives / negatives    (2 · train)
#   data/corpus/eval/   the TTS evaluation corpora         (3 · eval)
#   data/audit/         src/scripts/ one-off measurement output
#
#   output/             trained oww + mww models, training_config.yaml, scorecards
data/
output/

# Written by src/train/oww/train.py at the START of every run and handed to
# openwakeword as --training_config. Purely intermediate: nothing else reads it, and
# the next run overwrites it - so as a record of "what produced this model" it only
# ever describes whichever run finished last.
#
# It also embeds ABSOLUTE paths (corpus_dir, output_dir), which differ between the
# Mac and the CUDA box, so tracking it makes the two machines overwrite each other's
# copy forever.
#
# Provenance is covered instead by the run tag - <commit>-d<audio hash>, see
# src/train/provenance.py - which ties settings to the artefact rather than to the clock.
training_config.yaml

# Virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
.venv-*/

# The openWakeWord clone that src/scripts/setup-applesilicon-trainer.sh makes under
# src/train/. It is upstream's code plus our patches applied in place - reproducible from
# that script, and never ours to commit. src/train/oww/train.py resolves it as
# OWW_CLONE (src/train/openwakeword/...), which is why it sits there rather than out of
# the way. The pattern has no leading slash, so it matches at this depth and anywhere
# else the clone moves to. .dockerignore excludes it too: inside a build context it
# would shadow the clone each image makes for itself, with one patched for a
# different device.
openwakeword/

# The microWakeWord clone that src/scripts/setup-mww-applesilicon-trainer.sh makes under
# src/train/, pinned to one commit of OHF-Voice/micro-wake-word. The venv in
# src/train/train-mww-applesilicon/ installs it editable, so HEAD is state - .dockerignore
# excludes it for the same reason as openwakeword/.
# (No leading slash: the pattern matches at any depth, wherever the clone lives.)
microwakeword/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
# uv build artifacts from src/tts-service/tts_protocol.
**/build/

# OS / IDE / archives
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.zip
.claude/settings.json

# training logs - one per run, written by the run-*.sh scripts into logs/
# `logs/*` rather than `logs/` so the score curves can be re-included: git does not
# descend into an excluded directory, so a negation under `logs/` would do nothing.
# THIS BRANCH ONLY: main ignores all of logs/, because main carries no records.
logs/*
# The curve CSVs are the evidence every deploy/scorecards.jsonl row cites (`curve`).
# Ignored, they make a row checkable only on the machine that wrote it - and the row is
# the published number. `score_margins.py --csv` writes them; they are text and small.
!logs/scorecurves/
*.log

# deployment staging dir: the RECORD is tracked, the blobs are not.
# `deploy/` ignored the whole directory, which meant the file that says what is staged and
# what the rules for changing it are - deploy/README.md - lived outside version control, so
# its own "corrections are errata in git history" rule was unsatisfiable. No model binary is
# tracked anywhere in this repo, so ignore the weights and keep the markdown, the row-per-
# measurement JSONL and the ESPHome/LVA manifests, which are text and are diffable.
deploy/**/*.tflite
deploy/**/*.onnx